      "body": "Perfect! Here\u2019s a **text-based diagram** illustrating how the data transformation happens for this code \u2014 especially around the `groupby` and `aggregation` steps.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\uddf1 Step-by-step Diagram of Data Flow\n\n#### **Initial DataFrame (`df`)**\n| product_category | product_id | rating |\n|:-----------------|:------------|:--------|\n| Electronics       | E01         | 5 |\n| Electronics       | E02         | 2 |\n| Electronics       | E01         | 3 |\n| Clothing          | C01         | 1 |\n| Clothing          | C02         | 4 |\n\n---\n\n#### **Step 1: Add `sentiment_category`**\n(using `pd.cut` on `rating`)\n\n| product_category | product_id | rating | sentiment_category |\n|:-----------------|:------------|:--------|:-------------------|\n| Electronics       | E01         | 5 | Positive |\n| Electronics       | E02         | 2 | Negative |\n| Electronics       | E01         | 3 | Neutral |\n| Clothing          | C01         | 1 | Negative |\n| Clothing          | C02         | 4 | Positive |\n\n---\n\n#### **Step 2: Group by `product_category` and `sentiment_category`**\n\nGrouping produces **buckets** of rows like:\n\n```\nElectronics \u2192 Positive  \u2192 [rows with E01, rating=5]\nElectronics \u2192 Neutral   \u2192 [rows with E01, rating=3]\nElectronics \u2192 Negative  \u2192 [rows with E02, rating=2]\nClothing    \u2192 Positive  \u2192 [rows with C02, rating=4]\nClothing    \u2192 Negative  \u2192 [rows with C01, rating=1]\n```\n\nThen `.agg()` runs inside each bucket to compute:\n\n- `rating_count` = total number of rows\n- `product_id_nunique` = number of distinct `product_id`s\n\n---\n\n#### **Step 3: Aggregated Result (`analysis` DataFrame)**\n\n| product_category | sentiment_category | rating_count | product_id_nunique |\n|:-----------------|:-------------------|:--------------|:--------------------|\n| Electronics       | Positive | 1 | 1 |\n| Electronics       | Neutral  | 1 | 1 |\n| Electronics       | Negative | 1 | 1 |\n| Clothing          | Positive | 1 | 1 |\n| Clothing          | Negative | 1 | 1 |\n\n---\n\n#### **Step 4: Compute % of Negative Reviews**\n(using total counts and negative counts)\n\n| product_category | total_reviews | negative_reviews | negative_pct |\n|:-----------------|:--------------|:-----------------|:--------------|\n| Electronics       | 3 | 1 | \\(1 / 3 \\times 100 = 33.3\\%\\) |\n| Clothing          | 2 | 1 | \\(1 / 2 \\times 100 = 50.0\\%\\) |\n\n---\n\n#### **Visualization Summary**\n```\n   \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n   \u2502   Original DataFrame    \u2502\n   \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                \u2193\n   + Add computed column: sentiment_category\n                \u2193\n   \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n   \u2502   Group by category+sentiment\u2502\n   \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                \u2193\n   + Aggregate counts (rating_count, product_id_nunique)\n                \u2193\n   \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n   \u2502     Aggregated table    \u2502\n   \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                \u2193\n   + Compute per-category % of negative reviews\n                \u2193\n   \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n   \u2502        Final Output     \u2502\n   \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to generate a **visual diagram (graphical flow using Plotly or matplotlib shapes)** that shows this transformation as an image you can display inline in JupyterLab?"
